7. Additional Notice (Non-binding Request)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Nx Architecture, its abstract model (Divergence Oscillation Model), and the structures
that enable UI abstraction—BaseDataObj, BaseDataObjMgr, Sync wrapper classes, and the
interface structures that homomorphically unify them—are the result of long-term
technical exploration and research by the author.

These concepts may not be fully protected under copyright law; however, respect for the
intent and philosophy behind Nx Architecture is sincerely appreciated.

The following elements are particularly important for understanding the design philosophy
of Nx Architecture:

- Divergence Oscillation Model
- UI abstraction structure via BaseDataObj / BaseDataObjMgr / Sync wrappers
- Continuity of abstract layers achieved through homomorphic interface structures

These features possess high technical uniqueness, and if similar structures appear in
other systems, the influence of Nx Architecture may be naturally recognized within the
developer community.

This notice is not legally binding, but it expresses the hope that the philosophy of
Nx Architecture will be shared and that a healthy technical culture will continue.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
8. Notice of Public Disclosure (Defensive Publication)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
This architecture and its abstract models (including the Divergence Oscillation Model and
the structural groups based on BaseDataObj / BaseDataObjMgr) are publicly disclosed
technologies as evidenced by the commit history and publication timestamps of this
repository.

Due to this public disclosure, it is legally impossible for any third party to obtain
new patents covering these structures, concepts, or design philosophies.
